From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:31:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the S_SPI0 controller

The SoC dtsi describes no SPI controller of the CPUS domain. A board that
brings S_SPI0 out on a pin header cannot use it.

Add S_SPI0 at 0x07092000 (A733 manual, memory map), interrupt SPI 210
(12.2.3.1). The manual gives its registers as the same as those of SPI0
(18.8.7), which is the binding's "allwinner,sun60i-a733-spi" compatible
with its fallback, so spi-sun6i binds to it. The node has the bus clock
and the reset of the PRCM (4.2.5.13) and the module clock S_SPI_CLK
(4.2.5.12), each with its own gate.

Add the pin group for clock, MOSI and MISO on PL5 to PL7, function 4
(18.14.3.1), which the Radxa Cubie A7S routes to pins 22, 13 and 15 of its
pin header. Chip select 0 (PL4) does not reach the header, so it is not in
the group and a board uses a GPIO chip select. The pins are shared with
S_UART0 and S_IR_RX, so a board uses one function on them. The node is
disabled; a board enables it.

Not covered: DMA requests.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the node enabled for a test and pins 13
and 15 of J11 joined, a spidev transfer longer than the FIFO comes back
unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 65c169758266..bd6c014147a8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1841,6 +1841,13 @@ r_uart0_pl6_pins: r-uart0-pl6-pins {
 				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
 				function = "s_uart0";
 			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_spi0_pl5_pins: r-spi0-pl5-pins {
+				pins = "PL5", "PL6", "PL7";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <4>;
+				function = "s_spi0";
+			};
 		};
 
 		r_ir: ir@7040000 {
@@ -1910,6 +1917,19 @@ rtc: rtc@7090000 {
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		r_spi0: spi@7092000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-spi",
+				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-spi";
+			reg = <0x07092000 0x1000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 210 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_SPI>, <&r_ccu CLK_R_SPI>;
+			clock-names = "ahb", "mod";
+			resets = <&r_ccu RST_BUS_R_SPI>;
+			status = "disabled";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+		};
+
 		cpu_ccu: clock-controller@8870000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu";
 			reg = <0x08870000 0x4000>;
